menu "Clarke Park Transform"

    config CLARKE_PARK_IQ_FORMAT
        int "IQmath Q-format (GLOBAL_IQ)"
        range 1 30
        default 15
        help
            Q-format used by the _iq backend. This value is applied as
            GLOBAL_IQ before including IQmathLib.h, so all _IQ() / _IQtoF()
            / _IQmpy() calls in clarke_park use this fractional bit count.

            The default is 15, the format of the CORDIC hardware, so the
            hardware accelerator (see CLARKE_PARK_USE_CORDIC_HW) can be used
            without changing the format.

            Typical choices:
              - 15 (default): matches the CORDIC hardware, approx. +/- 1 range.
              - 24         : higher precision, range approx. +/- 128.
              - 8          : very large range, lower precision.

            If your application #defines GLOBAL_IQ itself before including
            clarke_park.h, that value must match this option
            (CONFIG_CLARKE_PARK_IQ_FORMAT).

    config CLARKE_PARK_USE_CORDIC_HW
        bool "Use the hardware CORDIC accelerator for the Park transform"
        depends on SOC_CORDIC_SUPPORTED
        default n
        help
            When the chip has a CORDIC accelerator (currently ESP32-S3R,
            see the CORDIC peripheral driver documentation), use it to
            accelerate the sin/cos of the fixed-point Park transform.

            The CORDIC hardware only supports the Q15 fixed-point format,
            so this option only takes effect when CLARKE_PARK_IQ_FORMAT is
            15. With any other Q-format the component transparently falls
            back to the software IQmath implementation. The float backend is
            never affected.

            The CORDIC engine handle required by the driver is owned by the
            clarke_park component (there is only one hardware unit, so the
            handle is a singleton). If your application needs the CORDIC
            unit for other computations, it must coordinate with this
            component and must not create a second engine while the
            clarke_park engine is in use.

endmenu
